"For $q\\in[0,1]$, call a graph $J$ **$q$-sparse** if\n\n$$\n\\mathbb{E}_qX_I\\geq 1\\quad\\forall I\\subseteq J,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbb{E}_qX_I$ is the expected number of copies of $I$ in $G_{n,q}$. **Sparse-graph reformulation.** There is a fixed $K$ such that if $H$ is $q$-sparse and $p=Kq$, then\n\n$$\nN(H,F)<\\mathbb{E}_pX_F\\quad\\forall F\\subset H.\n$$\n\nThis is stated as an appealing restatement of the fractional expectation threshold conjecture, with the harmless convention change from threshold $1/2$ to $1$ noted in the source. It is therefore open together with that conjecture."